{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455298-aberrant-factions-from-first-edition-or-new-factions","id":1455298,"title":"[Aberrant] factions from first edition or new factions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-21T04:06:51-07:00","id":1455298,"title":"[Aberrant] factions from first edition or new factions","content":"I haven't found some factions that existed in first edition like the survivors that joined with scandalous league to form the Eden colony and other such extrasolar nova colonies. Also haven't found the demon nova cult which I can't remember the name of which ended making some sort of quantum monster in the desert.<br /> <br /> What factions would you like to bring back for second edition or what new factions would you like to create in the new edition even if they are only Sub groups of current factions that you think would be cool if interesting for the setting.<br /> <br /> The survivors were interesting in first edition though as far as I'm aware once they set up the remote base they didn't do or interact much with anyone until they decided to leave the planet with the aid of the scandalous league so I'm not sure how you would involve them in a standard aberrant game on earth. Unless you decided they left earth early to look for a new home and you could join them in their space journey which could be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-21T05:23:22-07:00","id":1455299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeonstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455298-aberrant-factions-from-first-edition-or-new-factions#post1455298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't found some factions that existed in first edition like the survivors that joined with scandalous league to form the Eden colony and other such extrasolar nova colonies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming you mean the Daedalus League here, I'm not sure what faction you're referring to. In 1e, the Daedalus League first appeared in the Aberrant Player's Guide, one of the final books for the line. The only book that came out after the APG was Aberrant: Underworld, and there's no group of survivors (survivors of what?) like you describe that I'm aware of in either of those two books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also haven't found the demon nova cult which I can't remember the name of which ended making some sort of quantum monster in the desert. </div> </div> </div>The Church of Astaroth don't really fit the tone of the new edition, but nothing's saying you can't have them out there.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-21T05:31:20-07:00","id":1455301,"title":"","content":"Oops my mistake I just looked up the group it not called the survivors it called the protectors. A group of novas and baselines who early in the nova age made a remote base in Antarctica, they were led by a nova called Thomas sering who was a survivallist. The details are in aberrant players guide page 177.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-22T12:22:27-07:00","id":1455392,"title":"","content":"I don't think the Protectors were ever confirmed to have been the founders of the Eden colony (Apollo Milliken mentioned someone different), though I imagine they might have done something similar. I do remember the report from the Directive spy indicating that he watched Cyrus Katrak touchdown on the Protector's compound so they absolutely met with the Deadalus league.<br /> <br /> The Scandalous League sounds like an awesome name for a Teragen faction under the Pandaimonion... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-24T00:51:58-07:00","id":1455489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455298-aberrant-factions-from-first-edition-or-new-factions?p=1455392#post1455392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Scandalous League sounds like an awesome name for a Teragen faction under the Pandaimonion... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm picturing a bunch of Nova sensualists who are all about *deliberate* rule-breaking. They've decided that all of human law and tradition and morality is not relevant to their new existence, and so they are deliberately exploring what 'forbidden' things should indeed be off-limits to their new species, and which are just 'old-fashioned ideas' that, at best, only apply to baselines.<br /> <br /> And not little things like 'forget to signal before you turn' or 'eat fish on a Sunday,' but sketchy stuff like 'sleep with your sibling' or 'eat human flesh.'<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23754-ian-turner","name":"Ian Turner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T06:01:19-07:00","id":1456227,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m still associating a lot of the factions to their first edition versions. But how many factions are actually anti nova now. Because in 1e there were a few that came across as being out to get novas like the directive, proteus, church of Michael archangel etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T06:30:25-07:00","id":1456230,"title":"","content":"Well, the original game's idea that Proteus was attempting to neuter Novas is gone, along with a lot of the paranoia that was in the original game. <br /> <br /> The Directive, likewise, is less paranoid this time around. They still engage Nova threats too the world; but this version doesn't assume that a Nova is a threat until proven benign; so they come across as much less hostile unless and until you demonstrate your own hostility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}